secubox-lyrion (1.1.3-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * lyrionctl: new `medialib` verb (detect | mount <path> | unmount | status),
    always JSON. `detect` enumerates external mountpoints (under /media, /mnt,
    /data/external + removable mounts from /proc/mounts) that CONTAIN audio
    files (mp3/flac/m4a/ogg/wav/aac) and returns them as candidates — it NEVER
    mounts. `mount <path>` (after the operator confirms in the webui) adds a
    READ-ONLY `lxc.mount.entry` binding <path> to medialib/external inside the
    Lyrion LXC, live-mounts it RO if the container runs, persists
    `external_medialib = "<path>"` in lyrion.toml so it re-binds on boot, and
    triggers an LMS rescan. `unmount` reverses all of it. Auto-detect +
    opt-in confirm — never mount blind.
  * api/main.py: JWT-gated (nginx auth_request) endpoints delegating to the ctl —
    GET /medialib (status + detected candidates), POST /medialib/mount ({path}),
    POST /medialib/unmount. Blocking ctl work (fs scan, bind, rescan) is offloaded
    to a worker thread to keep the shared event loop free.
  * www/lyrion/index.html: new "Médiathèque externe" panel — current mount +
    detected candidates with a per-candidate "Monter" (confirm → RO bind) button
    and a "Démonter" button for the active mount.

